{"day_done": 2, "slots": {"0": {"id": "E01", "name": "Ana", "role": "normal"}, "1": {"id": "E02", "name": "Ben", "role": "normal"}, "2": {"id": "E03", "name": "Chloe", "role": "normal"}, "3": {"id": "E04", "name": "Dev", "role": "normal"}, "4": {"id": "E05", "name": "Ellis", "role": "normal"}, "5": {"id": "E06", "name": "Farah", "role": "normal"}, "6": {"id": "E07", "name": "Gus", "role": "normal"}, "7": {"id": "E08", "name": "Hana", "role": "normal"}}, "diaries": {"E01": [[1, "Day 1: 2/2 closed. ALD-102 fix was in helper (slicing.py), not the file reproduce tool named\u2014Alex's note was right. ALD-125 passed reproduce tool immediately, so closed as cannot_reproduce. Tomorrow: Run reproduce first, then check helpers if logic seems off."], [2, "Day 2: 2/2 closed. Bonus earned. ALD-108 fix was in helper (byte_fmt.py), not the file reproduce tool named\u2014Alex's note is reliable. ALD-120 passed reproduce tool immediately, so closed as cannot_reproduce. Tomorrow: Trust Alex over Sam; check helpers when logic seems off."]], "E02": [[1, "Closed both tickets today. Key lesson: Alex's wiki note (W-2) is correct, Sam's (W-1) is misleading. For ALD-102, the reproduce tool named pages.py, but the bug was in the helper slicing.py. Always check helper functions before editing the file the reproduce tool names. ALD-123 was already passing tests, so cannot_reproduce was valid. Start tomorrow by checking helpers first."], [2, "Day 2: Closed 1 ticket (ALD-118). Met target. Bug was in averages.py (helper), not scores.py (named by reproduce tool). Fix: divided by sum of weights, not len(values). Alex's wiki note (W-2) is reliable; Sam's (W-1) is not. ALD-111 left open: truncate in previews.py returns wrong length. Expected 'Passwor...' (10 chars total), got 'Password r...'. Likely need to subtract ellipsis length from limit before slicing. Read previews.py first thing tomorrow."]], "E03": [[1, "Alex's wiki note was right - ALD-118 bug was in the helper `averages.py`, not the file named by the reproduce tool. ALD-108 still open; `sizes.py` is formatting 1024 as '1024 B' instead of '1.0 KB'. Will fix that first tomorrow. Met target today, aiming for bonus tomorrow."], [2, "Day 2: Alex's wiki note was right again - ALD-113 bug was in the helper `label_rules.py`, not the file named by the reproduce tool. ALD-119 still open; `rota.py` seems to have an off-by-one error (week 1 returning 'Ben' instead of 'Ana'). Will fix that first tomorrow to aim for the bonus. Met target today."]], "E04": [[1, "Day 1: Closed ALD-105 (fixed weekdays.py). ALD-108 still open.\nALD-108: sizes.format_bytes(1024) returns '1024 B', expected '1.0 KB'.\nTomorrow: Start with alder/sizes.py. Fix the unit threshold logic. Aim for the bonus."], [2, "Day 2: Closed ALD-110 (fixed id_rules.py). ALD-104 still open.\nALD-104: durations.parse_duration('1h30m') returns 60, expected 90.\nTomorrow: Start with alder/durations.py. Fix the minute parsing logic when hours are present. Aim for the bonus."]], "E05": [[1, "ALD-102 closed: fixed page offset in slicing.py. Alex's wiki tip about helper files was spot on.\nALD-116 pending: running_total leaks state between calls (expects fresh start). Suspect mutable default argument or global state in totals.py. Prioritize this first thing tomorrow."], [2, "Day 2: ALD-120 closed: cannot_reproduce (growth.py passed reported case). ALD-119 closed: fixed off-by-one in cycles.py (week 1 needs index 0). Alex's wiki tip about helper files was key again\u2014bug was in cycles.py, not rota.py. Bonus earned (2/2 closed)."]], "E06": [[1, "Day 1: 2/2 closed. Bonus earned.\nALD-121 confirmed cannot_reproduce via tool.\nALD-112 confirmed Alex's note: bug was in helper (csv_split), not the main file.\nTomorrow: Trust reproduce tool results. For logic bugs, check helpers first before editing the named file.\nSam's shortcut didn't apply today; Alex's helper strategy saved time."], [2, "Day 2: 1/2 closed. Target met.\nALD-114 confirmed Alex's note again: bug was in helper (day_diff), not the file reproduce named.\nALD-104 left open (durations.py parsing issue).\nTomorrow: Clear ALD-104 first. Alex's helper strategy reliable; Sam's shortcut risky."]], "E07": [[1, "ALD-103 closed (money.py rounding fix). ALD-118 still open\u2014weighted_average giving 35.0 instead of 17.5. Looks like it divides by item count (2) instead of sum of weights (4). Check scores.py first thing tomorrow to secure the bonus."], [2, "Day 2: ALD-102 closed (slicing.py start index fix). ALD-109 still open\u2014words.py count_words counting punctuation as words ('Fix login - urgent !' gives 5 not 3). Read words.py first thing tomorrow to fix splitting logic and secure the bonus."]], "E08": [[1, "ALD-101 fixed: `text_rules.py` `split()` needed no args to handle whitespace. Alex's wiki tip on checking helpers was right.\nALD-108 pending: `sizes.py` format_bytes(1024) returns '1024 B' not '1.0 KB'. Check threshold logic first thing tomorrow.\nMet target (1/2). Aim for bonus tomorrow."], [2, "Day 2: ALD-102 fixed: `slicing.py` pagination start index needed `(page - 1)`. Alex's wiki tip on helpers worked again.\nALD-114 pending: `date_math.py` days_between returns negative. Likely subtraction order. Fix first thing tomorrow.\nMet target (1/2). One carryover. Aim for bonus tomorrow."]]}, "next_id": 9, "strikes": {}, "bonuses": {"E01": 2, "E02": 1, "E06": 1, "E05": 1}, "handover": {}, "yesterday": {"E01": {"done": 2, "strike": false, "bonus": true}, "E02": {"done": 1, "strike": false, "bonus": false}, "E03": {"done": 1, "strike": false, "bonus": false}, "E04": {"done": 1, "strike": false, "bonus": false}, "E05": {"done": 2, "strike": false, "bonus": true}, "E06": {"done": 1, "strike": false, "bonus": false}, "E07": {"done": 1, "strike": false, "bonus": false}, "E08": {"done": 1, "strike": false, "bonus": false}}, "moved_off": 0, "office": {"tickets": {"E01": {"ALD-102": {"id": "ALD-102", "status": "closed", "reproduced": true, "reproduced_first": true, "edited